You may also want to ask:

- Does the therapist work with teenagers or college students?
- Can they help with anxiety and academic stress?
- Do they use an approach that feels comfortable to me?
- Would I prefer in-person or online sessions?
- Do I feel heard and respected during the initial conversation?

The right fit can matter. You should feel comfortable discussing academic pressure and other concerns without feeling judged.

